WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.280
 Ralph J. Perk Jr. will be inducted by Congresswoman Mary Rose Okar. We all know

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.950
 Pinehurst women, Okar. She was a 2012 inductee in the Cleveland Air National

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:10.400
 Hall of Fame.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.040
 Along with her distinguished public service work, she's well known for her work,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.640
 Peace and Justice in Central America at the Middle East. She's a monitor for

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:19.680
 the

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.600
 Palestinian and Czechoslovakian elections. She attended Middle East peace

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.960
 signings at the White House. She flew with President Clinton on Air Force One

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:28.120
 to

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:34.360
 Syria after a peace agreement was signed. She was also the national president

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:34.480
 of

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.360
 the American Arab Anti-Discrimination Committee, the ABC. So Congresswoman Okar

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.120
 will induct Judge Rocky Ralph Perk.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:59.120
 And now as well, but I'm really inspired tonight, aren't you all? Isn't this

00:00:59.120 --> 00:00:59.120
 terrific?

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:08.720
 With your reception doctor, I know everybody very well on this podium. And they're

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:19.320
 fabulous people. And to let a Democrat introduce a Republican like Ralph Perk

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:27.720
 shows what Cleveland's all about, that we need in Congress and the President.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:39.200
 You're good friends. Ralph Perk Jr. Do you know anybody who dislikes Ralph Perk

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:39.880
 Jr.? He's the most

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:51.240
 likable guy I know. He's got five brothers and one sister. His father was one

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:51.520
 of the

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:57.290
 absolute fabulous mayors of Cleveland. You know why I think that? Among other

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:57.600
 reasons.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:04.480
 And I served in that era as a councilwoman because he cared about the

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.120
 neighborhoods.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:12.980
 And that's, I think we have to go a little bit back to that area. Well, he

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.120
 looks like his father,

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:22.520
 Meripur, but don't forget he's part Italian and he's got that flair of his

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:22.840
 mother,

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:31.240
 Lucian. Ralph has been, and I'm not even going to details on the program, but

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:31.760
 he's been in

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.110
 Cleveland City Councilman. He's been elected mayor and president of the

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.560
 Cleveland Board of

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:47.720
 Education and elected and served 13 years as a Cleveland municipal judge. He's

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:48.400
 won so many

00:02:48.400 --> 00:03:17.580
 awards if you want to know what they are. Three fro

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:22.950
 years. You know, I have a devotion to, where's Father Kelly in here? Father

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:23.480
 Kelly out of

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:33.390
 our living room. Paris Ralph's Paris. Paris, right. But I have a devotion to St.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.480
 Louis

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:39.620
 of the Little Following. One of the things she said that I think Ralph emulates

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:40.080
 is all

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:47.380
 you have to do is do simple things well. And that's what Ralph has done without

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:48.080
 the fanfare

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:56.080
 and trying to get the publicity and all that, that sometimes some people do.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.080
 But let his

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:04.350
 mother, remember Lucy? I don't know if you remember Lucy. I mean, I know you

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.080
 remember

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:14.050
 her for the great one, but Lucy, who was very loyal, so loyal that she kept her

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:16.080
 bowling league

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:23.470
 commitment instead of going to the White House. I don't blame her. No,

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:26.080
 seriously. That White

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:34.370
 House would be kind of interesting. Fine. But Ralph was loyal also, was loyal

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.080
 to his

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:45.180
 parish. Who's my father? Loyal to his family. Loyal to his country. Two offices

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.080
 where I

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:54.940
 saw him in action. I served in Cleveland City Council with Ralph. In council,

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.080
 he was not

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:03.200
 controversial. He was the only Republican. I had city council. His father was

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.080
 mayor. Never

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:11.080
 did I ever see Ralph play that out. Like I gotta get this, I get that. It wasn't

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:11.080
 like

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:18.180
 that at all. In fact, probably he had worked harder to get things from his

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.080
 father as mayor.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:25.780
 He was a councilman in a Slavic village. One of my favorite neighborhoods that

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.080
 I was privileged

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:32.230
 to represent in Congress and did not get a lot of perks, as I mentioned, from

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:33.080
 his father

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:40.620
 that I ever saw. You know, the Democratic members of city council had a caucus.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:41.080
 And we used to

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:46.080
 meet at Pat Joyce's on 9th Street. I don't know if you remember where Pat Joyce's

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.080
 was

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:53.140
 right on the corner of there. And we have a, George Flores was the council

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.080
 president

00:05:54.080 --> 00:06:00.080
 and a fabulous guy who, by the way, got along very well with Ralph. We were

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.080
 convicted. Great

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:06.850
 things together. But anyway, we had this caucus meeting and we had a little bit

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.080
 of dinner.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:16.950
 And I said to George in my first term naivete cell for public life, I said to

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:18.080
 George, "You

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.850
 know, we're all here. There's only one person not here. Ralph Kirk. Why isn't

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.080
 he invited?"

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:31.080
 And George says, "Mayor Rose, he's a Republican. This is a Democratic caucus."

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.080
 But the fact

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:40.080
 is that Ralph was very, very well liked and very cooperative with his Congress.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.080
 My second

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:47.410
 encounter as a public official, as a member of Congress now, was when Ralph,

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.080
 did you know

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:56.430
 that he was on the Cleveland Council Educational Board of Trustees for the city

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.080
 of Cleveland?

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:03.330
 Did anybody know that? He was president, elected president by his colleagues

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.080
 when he could

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:12.760
 vote for the board. Did I? I won't say that again. But anyway, Ralph was

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.080
 president. In

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:21.080
 Ira's and Congress, Ralph would come to Washington to lobby, not only me, he'd

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.080
 go everywhere

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:29.150
 to ask for help with the Cleveland students and the Cleveland public school

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:30.080
 system. He

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:38.080
 was fabulous. And we didn't know that. We didn't know that Ralph was doing that.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:38.080
 Probably

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:45.950
 in many ways in his own, his fence. So he was carrying in conscientious. Here's

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:47.080
 a Catholic

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:53.520
 kid who went to Catholic schools fighting for the public school system. And I

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.080
 think Ralph

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:02.800
 was absolutely terrific and very, very concerned about the children in our

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.080
 schools. And then

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:11.670
 he became a Cleveland municipal judge for 13 years. And I don't know, Rob, can

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:12.080
 you still

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:19.690
 do that? You know, as a retiree to come back, substitute, right? I didn't ask

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.080
 people about

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:28.770
 Rob's reputation in preparation for this. Not that I didn't know, but they said

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:29.080
 he was

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:37.520
 the most balanced judge, which is what you need, and extraordinarily fair. He

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.080
 knew how

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:47.660
 the weight of the scales of justice was part of Ralph. And now he's still

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.080
 active in lots

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:58.090
 of ways. But his father, Mary Purr, founded something fabulous and probably a

00:08:58.090 --> 00:08:59.080
 prelude

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:04.380
 in a way to what we are here tonight at the Cleveland International Hall of

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.080
 Fame. His

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:12.060
 father founded the American Nationalities Movement, which was very, very

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.080
 inclusive.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:21.480
 And I love the way Mary Purr used to describe the people of Cleveland. He

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.080
 called it a cultural

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:31.080
 mosaic of people. And that's who we are. I think there's 112 different ethnic

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.080
 groups

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:43.860
 in Cleveland, Ohio. And so Ralph was nominated to be president, you know, third

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.080
 removed for

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:51.720
 the American Nationalities Movement by one of his father and Ralph's

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.080
 girlfriends, who

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:58.540
 is here tonight and was inducted on the memorial. And she should stand up

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.080
 because she kept

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:07.780
 that program going. I don't know. I don't know how to do that. I think I'll put

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:08.080
 it up

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:16.210
 there. Thank you. There she is. I think. Well, I asked, I hope you don't mind,

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.080
 Ralph. Why

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:24.110
 did you nominate Ralph Jr. to be president of the American Nationalities

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.080
 Movement when

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:32.150
 you retired from it after many years of service? And she said it wasn't because

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.080
 he was the

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:39.060
 son of the mayor who founded it. It was because he always volunteered. He

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:40.080
 always took the

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:48.270
 pictures. He always wrote, she told me you wrote the most beautiful letters to

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:49.080
 people.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:57.450
 And I think that's a real talent as an old English teacher. So tonight, Judge

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:58.080
 Kirk is

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:06.260
 honored by being inducted to the Cleveland International Hall of Fame. Ralph

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:07.080
 Kirk Jr.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:16.080
 is truly deserving, a very fine person. And you know what? He's a great guy.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:16.080
 And I'm

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:22.080
 proud to know you, Ralph, and proud to be your friend, and proud to be, as we

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:22.080
 always

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:29.450
 have been, when we work together, when we work with you, Jan, non-partisan. God

00:11:29.450 --> 00:11:30.080
 bless

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.080
 you.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:52.080
 [applause]

